main = draw x = Uniform in if Uniform < 0.5 then x else x + 1.0
-- An `if` condition that draws fresh randomness independent of the bound
-- variable: an even mixture of Uniform and Uniform + 1, a flat density of 0.5
-- on (0, 2). Was a known issue (the set-witness engine refused the fresh
-- condition); answered since task world-residual-factor-delegation splits
-- the worlds by the condition's two polarity masses. The point 1.0 itself is
-- avoided: both closed supports contain it, so it reads 1.0 there, a
-- measure-zero boundary artifact.
